  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the maximum magnitude outcome (i.e., the highest prize) and its probability, favoring the lottery where this outcome has a more favorable (higher) weighted value. However, the individual does not emphasize the highest prize or compare the 2500-Euro outcome in B to the 2400-Euro outcome in A in terms of their magnitude and likelihood. Instead, the individual focuses on the trade-off between a higher chance of winning any amount and avoiding the zero outcome, which reflects a sensitivity to the probability of non-zero outcomes rather than the maximum outcome weighted by its probability. The information considered by the individual (probability of winning something vs. nothing, small outcome difference) does not align with the information required by the decision reason (maximum outcome and its probability). Similarly, the justification (favoring higher chance of winning something) does not match the rule of the decision reason (favoring higher weighted maximum outcome). Therefore, the individual did not use this decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
